mga: the G450's memory after a drawing-engine soft reset (local patch 0129)

On a real G450 (bench F, 2026-11-16; RetroGPU docs/g450-memory.md) a soft reset (RST bit 0) leaves the DDR
memory uninitialised until the memory reset command (MACCESS bit 15, the last step of Linux matroxfb's
g450_memory_init): the first 16-bit word of every 8 bytes reads 0 at once, and with no refresh all of VRAM
decays within ~3 s. Modelled: after a G450's soft reset the CPU's linear reads of those words return 0 and
VRAM turns to noise every 2 s of emulated time, reported as MGA-HAZARD g450-memory once VRAM is used in that state, until a MACCESS write
with bit 15 set. The G450 also reports revision 85h, as bench F's card, and boots bench F's own BIOS when the
local ROM set has it (roms/video/matrox/mgaglide/g450-benchf.bin, read from the card with RetroGPU's ROMDUMP;
Matrox's code: local only, never in a repository): its PInS v5 block carries the memory values the HAL's set-up
reads, where 935-20's PInS is blank (version 0). The G400's SGRAM keeps its contents through a reset, as before.

